# Decision Log — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

> A hook auto-logs AskUserQuestion decisions to `DECISIONS.inbox.md` (raw, untriaged drafts) as they happen; the commit gate reminds when the inbox has undigested drafts. Claude then triages: key decisions (technology choices, trade-offs, plan reversals, workarounds) get distilled into the structured records below, newest first; requirement-shaped entries move to the `REQUIREMENTS.md` goal inbox; noise is discarded.
> Entry format: `## Date - type(scope): title` + **What / Why / Changes**, with optional **Known limitation / Out of scope / Deferred**.
> Type reference: arch (architecture) / decision (product or technical trade-off) / feat / fix. Numbering cross-references `REQUIREMENTS.md`'s "Confirmed Decisions" in both directions.

## {{DATE}} - arch(stack): Adopted the team's Go baseline stack

**What**: Backend Go 1.25 (net/http + chi + pgx + golang-migrate), database {{DATABASE}}; full baseline in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` section 1.

**Why**: The team's backend baseline is fixed to Go (native concurrency, single static binary, stateless horizontal scaling) — no per-project stack selection; switching stacks requires first amending the /scaffold baseline table.

**Changes**: Written to disk by /scaffold initialization; the ARCHITECTURE.md tech stack table is pre-filled per the baseline.
